Subject: [PATCH] docs: the public trail for the b10680 kernel wave - lanes
 202, 204 and 209

Documentation only. No source file is touched, no default moves, and no number
here is new: every figure is transcribed from a measurement already banked under
research/local-inference/lane-evidence/ or in the cited commit's own message.

CHANGELOG.md gains a section for upstream base b10680 with a per-mechanism
BEFORE/AFTER table and a per-model-file table, then one entry per mechanism:
the dedicated iq4_xs mat-vec (+12% drafted on UD-IQ4_XS), the gated iq3_s split
(+11% drafted on UD-Q3_K_XL, and the superseded every-width build listed with
its 7-9% loss), the ROCmFP4-FAST mat-mat pipelines (prefill 16112 -> 4683 ms),
the ROCmFP4-FAST MMVQ mat-vec (+27% drafted, integration BLOCKED), the tiled
concat-transpose (-13% on the op, TIED at the seat, twice), the q6_k direct
scales (MEASURED NEUTRAL, never to be quoted as a win), --spec-draft-adaptive
(UNMEASURED here; its table is upstream-reported on a Radeon 8060S and is not
restated as ours) and the draft-replay server fix.

Three rules of that file are load-bearing here and were applied rather than
assumed. Every row names its own BEFORE binary, AFTER binary, model file and
measurement epoch, because a driver update, a reboot and a RAM change separate
the runs and their absolutes must never be differenced. Neutral, superseded and
blocked mechanisms are listed with their numbers, not omitted. And a new closing
subsection states where each commit actually is: only 5b1b416cb is on the
default branch today.

docs/FINDINGS.md gains five rows. F-13: a kernel that passes test-backend-ops
can still flip the first token to end-of-generation - three falsified hypotheses
and the width the defect was finally isolated to. F-14: the per-row barrier was
the leading explanation for the ~35% q6_K bandwidth deficit and is falsified;
the deficit is open, and the motivating q4_K figure is corrected. F-15: this
box's undrafted decode is bimodal and the cell-wise mean follows the slow
rounds, which is why plain verdicts are read from the median. F-16: a serve-line
presence penalty inherited by a request that omitted it manufactured empty
completions, which is what made F-13 attributable once fixed. F-17: why commit
provenance alone does not stop a rebase from deleting a measured result. Open
questions gains five entries.

docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md gains four rows: GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE,
GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES (which defaults ON, inverting this registry's usual
shape, and says so), the ROCmFP4-FAST MMVQ width gate - recorded as code with
NO new environment variable, cross-referencing the pre-existing upstream
GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ rather than inventing a fork lever - and
--spec-draft-adaptive.

patches/series/PENDING-ROWS.md is new and hand-written, and is the only
hand-written file in that directory. series regen still stops on ten
pre-existing merge commits, so the rows it will emit are staged there in the
generator's format instead of being hand-edited into the generated MANIFEST.md,
which would produce a green-looking artifact that dies at the next git am. It is
invisible to the tooling (patch enumeration matches ^\d{4}-.*\.patch$) and is
superseded the moment regen runs.

One divergence from the assignment is recorded rather than quietly resolved: it
described the rank-7 empty completion as a file/prompt defect rather than a
kernel one. The lane evidence says otherwise - forcing the float path removed
the empties, and removing width 2 repaired them - so F-13 follows the evidence.

